messages[14]{user,text}:
  user_2,[00:02] Hello, am I speaking with Neha Chauhan?
  user_1,[00:09] Umm, yes. Hi. Who is this?
  user_2,[00:12] Hi Neha, this is Karan Joshi calling from Safe Step Insurance on behalf of DCoders. I'm following up on the email we sent you regarding your health policy -- um, policy number HLTH-883921.
  user_1,[00:30] Oh, right. The email about the renewal. Look, [sighs] to be honest with you Karan, I'm not looking to renew it.
  user_2,[00:41] Ah, I see. May I know the reason, Neha? Is it because of the premium adjustment, or did you find coverage elsewhere?
  user_1,[00:48] No, nothing like that. It's just... I actually switched jobs last month, and my new employer provides a corporate health cover that takes care of everything. So I really don't need this personal policy anymore.
  user_2,[01:08] [typing] Got it, understood. That makes total sense if your new company has comprehensive coverage. Congratulations on the new job, by the way!
  user_1,[01:17] Thank you! Yeah, it's a good move. So do I need to fill out any forms to cancel, or how does this work?
  user_2,[01:25] Well, actually, your policy grace period ended last week, so technically it's already sitting in a pending-expiry status in our system. Since you don't want to renew it, I just need your verbal confirmation to officially let it lapse and move the status to 'Expired'. No paperwork needed from your end.
  user_1,[01:52] Oh, perfect! Yeah, just let it expire. I definitely don't want to pay for another term.
  user_2,[02:00] [typing] Sure thing. I am updating the system right now... okay, policy HLTH-883921 has now been marked as Expired. You won't be charged anything further.
  user_1,[02:22] Awesome. Thank you so much for clearing that up quickly, Karan.
  user_2,[02:28] Anytime, Neha! If you ever need personal coverage in the future, you know where to find us. Have a wonderful week ahead!
  user_1,[02:37] Thanks, you too. Bye!